<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n44431" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εὔμᾱρις</span></b>  [later <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ᾰ</span> (v. infr.)], <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ιδος</span>, ἡ, acc. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b>
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εὔμᾱριν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					A.
					<u>Pers.</u>
					660
				</span></i>
			 (lyr.); but acc. pl. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εὐμᾱρίδας</span> (sic) <i><span class="en">
				Lyc.
				855
			</span></i> (on the accent, v. Hdn.Gr.<i><span class="en">
				1.99
			</span></i>): —<i>an Asiatic shoe</i> or <i>slipper</i>
			(made of deerskin, <i><span class="en">
				Poll.
				7.90
			</span></i>), 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">βαρβάροις ἐν εὐμάρισι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					E.
					<u>Or.</u>
					1370
				</span></i>
			 (lyr.); <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κροκόβαπτον . . εὔμαριν
				ἀείρων</span> A.l.c.; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">βαθύπελμος εὔμᾰρις</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>AP</u>
					7.413
				</span></i>
			 (Antip.), cf. Lyc.l.c. (Prob. a foreign word.)</div>
